[pruned 2026-06-30] - [uses: 1] Residual-delta measurement (not the headline +1.75): isolate active-research as the SOLE changed variable vs the Phase-55 baseline; part of +1.75 was already banked by Phase 55's spec reform (double-count guard). Subtraction test: ~0/negative residual is acceptable → keep/trim/cut. An LLM-executed skill step can't be scored by the binary eval runner, so a with-vs-without measurement artifact IS its functional test. Phase 58 result: +0.5 composite n=1 (reasoning 3→4), on a research-favorable topic — at the significance threshold with unknown variance; directional, not banked. Phase 59 strengthened it (3 new topics, 13 paired runs at n≥3, escalation + variance gate): the +0.5 did NOT replicate — all n≥3 deltas were ≤0 (poor −1.0 real, rich 0.0/−0.4 variance-dominated) ⇒ feature CUT. Method validated itself: the pre-registered poor-topic veto + variance gate turned an n=1 false-positive into an honest negative.
